From b643229bdf64b6bfc91bb716ae4970f142b896d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 04:55:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 279/283] fix(execution): anchor region guarantees and
 round-trip boundary/zero-input regions

Round-2 fixes for verify-0049-u5-region, based on integration tip 41ae82a01.

* region_digest now hashes the full per-operation entry (selected,
  numeric_guarantee, precision/envelope projections, fallback, bound and the
  provider metadata) instead of only the single-op plan digest; replay also
  compares selected / numeric_guarantee / fallback field-by-field against the
  plan_operation payload, so a rewritten guarantee is refused even after the
  public digest is re-signed.  Forging exp's precision to exact/proven now
  fails with region_digest_mismatch, and with a re-signed digest with
  region_numeric_guarantee_payload_mismatch; erasing fallback events fails
  with region_fallback_payload_mismatch.
* Region operations are renumbered to region-local 0..N-1; boundary entry
  inputs record source=outside_region_operation with producer_op_index=null
  and exit producers use the region-local index.  Boundary plans now
  validate / load / explain; a subgraph starting at a later global op also
  round-trips.
* Request validation is driven by the opcode contract arity, so zero-operand
  opcodes (iota) round-trip; request.op / roles / arity are cross-checked.
* plan_region runs validate_region_plan(re_resolve=False) on its own output
  before returning: a self-produced document that cannot be loaded is now a
  plan-time failure (covers boundary numbering, zero-input ops, empty
  selections).
* compose_region_precision derives the portable_bitwise statement from the
  actual provider set (no hard-coded "every op portable trunk"), and the
  is_upper_bound gate now requires reference consistency across every term,
  including zero-bound exact terms.
* capability_for_policy probes the host lazily: an explicitly supplied
  capability is accepted without /proc/cpuinfo or pinned-library dlopen.
* Nested operation regions and block regions are refused
  (region_nested_region_not_supported / region_block_region_not_supported)
  instead of being flattened into a plan that cannot express their scope.

Single-op plan digests stay byte-identical to the 923a72e26 baseline
(matmul f32/bf16 e0d1287e/7e95c65c, qmatmul 1717a8e5; plan_operation
delegation unchanged).  Tests: 33 region tests (including the verifier's
precision-forgery / iota / boundary repros as equivalents), 276 with the
existing execution suite.

(cherry picked from commit 85a1bab1b6c46f7ad8d16da191fda5e2df76cc8e)
